{"ld": 1835, "paper": "SP717", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Improve Nonemergency MaineCare Transportation", "sponsor_id": "s-bennett-richard", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-griffin-abigail", "h-matlack-ann", "h-mcintyre-mathew", "s-moore-marianne", "h-roeder-amy", "h-shagoury-daniel", "s-tipping-michael"], "committee_code": "HHS", "committee_name": "Health and Human Services", "summary": {"text": "This bill does the following.\n\n1. It requires the Department of Health and Human Services to create and maintain a MaineCare nonemergency transportation dashboard, which is information posted on the department's publicly accessible website reflecting broker performance indicators and results.\n\n2. It requires the department to track nonemergency transportation trips by region and categorize and issue a monthly report regarding all incidents involving the delivery on nonemergency transportation.\n\n3. It establishes the nonemergency transportation ombudsman program as an independent program within the Executive Department to provide ombudsman services to MaineCare members regarding MaineCare nonemergency transportation provided by the department.\n\n4. It requires the department to establish a nonemergency transportation advisory committee in each region to provide the department with recommendations regarding the performance of nonemergency transportation services in that region.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0717&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "died", "status_label": "Ought Not to Pass Pursuant To Joint Rule 310", "final_disposition": {"label": "Ought Not to Pass Pursuant To Joint Rule 310", "date": "2026-02-24", "governor_action": null, "governor_action_date": null}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1835)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0717&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}], "amendments": [], "committee_actions": [{"da